      "type": "text",
      "text": "(\n    <div style={{ backgroundColor: 'var(--color-background)', boxSizing: 'border-box', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', fontSize: '12px', fontSynthesis: 'none', gap: '40px', height: 'fit-content', lineHeight: '16px', MozOsxFontSmoothing: 'grayscale', overflow: 'clip', overflowWrap: 'anywhere', padding: '48px', WebkitFontSmoothing: 'antialiased', width: '1800px' }}>\n      <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: '8px' }}>\n        <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'var(--color-foreground)', fontFamily: '\"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif', fontSize: '30px', fontWeight: 600, letterSpacing: '-0.025em', lineHeight: '36px' }}>\n          YourProfiles\n        </div>\n        <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'var(--color-muted-foreground)', fontFamily: '\"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif', fontSize: '16px', lineHeight: '24px', whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap', width: '900px' }}>\n          Under review. One list of profiles, used in two places.<br />On the aggregate site the Profile tab opens it as a bottom sheet on phone and a modal on desktop: each community the person belongs to is a heading, with their profiles in it underneath, and tapping a profile opens it. A person with one profile in total never sees this; the tab opens that profile directly. On a community's own domain the tab shows only that community's profiles, with no heading.<br />On a community page the profile button in the banner opens the same list for that community only, and only when the person has several profiles there: a check marks the one in use, and tapping another switches to it. With one profile the button opens that profile.<br />A profile is labelled by its handle if it has one, otherwise its name, otherwise \"User\" and six characters. Private: nobody else can see these profiles together.<br />To decide: whether Settings belongs here.\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div style={{ alignItems: 'start', boxSizing: 'border-box', display: 'flex', gap: '48px' }}>\n        <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: '16px' }}>\n          <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'var(--color-muted-foreground)', fontFamily: '\"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif', fontSize: '16px', fontWeight: 500, letterSpacing: '0.03em', lineHeight: '20px', textTransform: 'uppercase' }}>\n            Phone: Profile on Home\n          </div>\n          <div style={{ backgroundImage: 'linear-gradient(in oklab 180deg, oklab(52% 0.006 0.010) 0%, oklab(34% 0.023 0.019) 100%)', backgroundOrigin: 'border-box', borderColor: 'var(--color-border-soft)', borderStyle: 'solid', borderWidth: '1px', boxSizing: 'border-box', flexShrink: '0', height: '844px', overflow: 'clip', position: 'relative', width: '390px' }}>\n            <div style={{ backgroundImage: 'linear-gradient(in oklab 180deg, oklab(0% 0 0 / 50%) 0%, oklab(0% 0 0 / 0%) 100%)', boxSizing: 'border-box', height: '96px', left: '0px', position: 'absolute', top: '0px', width: '100%' }} />\n            <div style={{ bottom: '64px', boxSizing: 'border-box', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: '4px', left: '0px', paddingBlock: '24px', paddingLeft: '24px', paddingRight: '80px', position: 'absolute', right: '0px' }}>\n              <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'var(--color-primary-foreground)', display: 'inline-block', fontFamily: '\"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif', fontSize: '18px', fontWeight: 600, lineHeight: '28px' }}>\n                @wavemaker\n              </div>\n              <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'color-mix(var(--color-primary-foreground) 90%, transparent)', display: 'inline-block', fontFamily: '\"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif', fontSize: '16px', lineHeight: '20px' }}>\n                Late-night loop, take two.\n              </div>\n              <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'color-mix(var(--color-primary-foreground) 70%, t